{"responses_create_params": {"input": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are a helpful and harmless assistant. You should think step-by-step before responding to the instruction below.\n\nPlease use python programming language only.\n\nYou must use ```python for just the final solution code block with the following format:\n```python\n# Your code here\n```\n\nMisha has a square $$$n \\times n$$$ matrix, where the number in row $$$i$$$ and column $$$j$$$ is equal to $$$a_{i, j}$$$. Misha wants to modify the matrix to contain exactly $$$k$$$ distinct integers. To achieve this goal, Misha can perform the following operation zero or more times:\n\n1. choose any square submatrix of the matrix (you choose $$$(x_1,y_1)$$$, $$$(x_2,y_2)$$$, such that $$$x_1 \\leq x_2$$$, $$$y_1 \\leq y_2$$$, $$$x_2 - x_1 = y_2 - y_1$$$, then submatrix is a set of cells with coordinates $$$(x, y)$$$, such that $$$x_1 \\leq x \\leq x_2$$$, $$$y_1 \\leq y \\leq y_2$$$),\n2. choose an integer $$$k$$$, where $$$1 \\leq k \\leq n^2$$$,\n3. replace all integers in the submatrix with $$$k$$$.\n\nPlease find the minimum number of operations that Misha needs to achieve his goal.\n\nInput\n\nThe first input line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 500, 1 \\leq k \\leq n^2$$$)  — the size of the matrix and the desired amount of distinct elements in the matrix.\n\nThen $$$n$$$ lines follows. The $$$i$$$-th of them contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_{i, 1}, a_{i, 2}, \\ldots, a_{i, n}$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_{i,j} \\leq n^2$$$) — the elements of the $$$i$$$-th row of the matrix.\n\nOutput\n\nOutput one integer — the minimum number of operations required.\n\nExamples\n\nInput\n\n3 4\n1 1 1\n1 1 2\n3 4 5\n\nOutput\n\n1\n\nInput\n\n3 2\n2 1 3\n2 1 1\n3 1 2\n\nOutput\n\n2\n\nInput\n\n3 3\n1 1 1\n1 1 2\n2 2 2\n\nOutput\n\n1\n\nInput\n\n3 2\n1 1 1\n1 2 1\n2 2 2\n\nOutput\n\n0\n\nNote\n\nIn the first test case the answer is $$$1$$$, because one can change the value in the bottom right corner of the matrix to $$$1$$$. The resulting matrix can be found below:\n\n111112341\n\nIn the second test case the answer is $$$2$$$. First, one can change the entire matrix to contain only $$$1$$$s, and the change the value of any single cell to $$$2$$$. One of the possible resulting matrices is displayed below:\n\n111111112"}]}, "verifier_metadata": {"unit_tests": {"inputs": ["3 4\r\n1 1 1\r\n1 1 2\r\n3 4 5\r\n", "3 2\r\n2 1 3\r\n2 1 1\r\n3 1 2\r\n", "3 3\r\n1 1 1\r\n1 1 2\r\n2 2 2\r\n", "3 2\r\n1 1 1\r\n1 2 1\r\n2 2 2\r\n", "1 1\r\n1\r\n", "3 5\r\n1 2 3\r\n4 5 6\r\n7 8 9\r\n", "5 7\r\n6 8 9 7 1\r\n8 10 11 8 2\r\n9 11 10 9 3\r\n7 8 9 6 4\r\n1 2 3 4 5\r\n", "2 2\r\n4 1\r\n2 3\r\n"], "outputs": ["1", "2", "1", "0", "0", "1", "2", "2"]}}, "hash_id": "17c5545cedfdf2f68ad41b91bdab0587", "dataset": "nano_v3_sft_profiled_comp_coding_50tests", "source": "codeforces", "agent_ref": {"type": "responses_api_agents", "name": "code_gen_lang_simple_agent"}, "pass_rate": 0.25, "language": "en"}
{"responses_create_params": {"input": [{"role": "user", "content": "你是一個有幫助且無害的助手。在回應以下指令之前，你應該要一步一步地思考。\n\n請只使用 python 程式語言。\n\n你必須使用 ```python 來包裹最終的解答程式碼區塊，格式如下：\n```python\n# Your code here\n```\n\n有 $k$ 個 sensor 位於一個 $n \\times m$ 米的長方形房間內。第 $i$ 個 sensor 位處於點 $(x_i, y_i)$。所有 sensor 均位於房間內不同的位置，且絕對不會在邊界上。\n\n房間的對角頂點分別位於 $(0, 0)$ 與 $(n, m)$，而房間的牆壁與座標軸平行。\n\n在時間 0 時，由點 $(0, 0)$ 發射一條 laser ray，方向朝向 $(1, 1)$。該 ray 以 $\\sqrt{2}$ 米每秒的速度行進，因此該 ray 在開始之後 1 秒就會到達點 $(1, 1)$。\n\n當該 ray 遇到牆壁時，會按照入射角等於反射角的規則進行反射；如果該 ray 行進到其中一個角落，就會立即停止。\n\n對於每個 sensor，你需要確定該 ray 第一次經過其所在位置時的時間。如果該 ray 根本不會經過該點，則輸出 -1。\n\nInput\n輸入的第一行包含三個整數 $n, m$ 及 $k$ ($2 \\le n, m \\le 100,000, 1 \\le k \\le 100,000$)，代表房間的牆長度及 sensor 的數量。\n隨後的 $k$ 行中，每一行都包含兩個整數 $x_i$ 及 $y_i$ ($1 \\le x_i \\le n - 1, 1 \\le y_i \\le m - 1$)，代表 sensor 的座標。保證沒有任何兩個 sensor 會在同一個點。\n\nOutput\n輸出 $k$ 個整數，第 $i$ 個整數代表該 ray 第一次經過該 sensor 所需的秒數，如果永遠不會經過則輸出 -1。\n\n例子\n\nInput\n3 3 4\n1 1\n1 2\n2 1\n2 2\n\nOutput\n1\n-1\n-1\n2\n\nInput\n3 4 6\n1 1\n2 1\n1 2\n2 2\n1 3\n2 3\n\nOutput\n1\n-1\n-1\n2\n5\n-1\n\nInput\n7 4 5\n1 3\n2 2\n5 1\n5 3\n4 3\n\nOutput\n13\n2\n9\n5\n-1\n\n註解\n在第一個樣本中，該 ray 會依序經過 $(0, 0)、(1, 1)、(2, 2)、(3, 3)$ 這些點。因此它會在 $(3, 3)$ 點停止，耗時 3 秒。\n\n在第二個樣本中，該 ray 會依序經過以下這些點：$(0, 0)、(1, 1)、(2, 2)、(3, 3)、(2, 4)、(1, 3)、(0, 2)、(1, 1)、(2, 0)、(3, 1)、(2, 2)、(1, 3)、(0, 4)$。該 ray 會在 $(0, 4)$ 點停止，耗時 12 秒。它會在 $(3, 3)、(2, 4)、(0, 2)、(2, 0)$ 及 $(3, 1)$ 這些點反射。"}]}, "verifier_metadata": {"unit_tests": {"inputs": ["3 3 4\n1 1\n1 2\n2 1\n2 2\n", "3 4 6\n1 1\n2 1\n1 2\n2 2\n1 3\n2 3\n", "7 4 5\n1 3\n2 2\n5 1\n5 3\n4 3\n", "10 10 10\n3 8\n1 7\n2 3\n4 2\n4 8\n3 3\n2 8\n5 5\n6 3\n3 1\n", "3 3 4\n1 1\n1 0\n2 1\n2 2\n", "10 10 10\n3 8\n1 7\n2 3\n4 2\n4 8\n3 3\n2 8\n5 6\n6 3\n3 1\n", "3 4 6\n1 1\n0 1\n1 2\n2 2\n1 3\n2 3\n", "7 4 5\n2 3\n2 2\n5 1\n5 3\n4 3\n", "10 10 10\n3 8\n1 7\n2 3\n4 2\n4 8\n5 3\n2 8\n5 6\n6 3\n3 1\n", "10 17 10\n3 8\n1 7\n2 3\n5 2\n4 8\n5 3\n2 8\n5 6\n6 3\n3 1\n", "10 17 10\n1 8\n1 7\n2 3\n7 2\n4 8\n5 3\n2 8\n8 6\n6 3\n3 1\n",